{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Evaluation: Benchmarks, Evals, LM Harness Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: A Minimal Eval Framework"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Define the core abstractions. An eval case has an input, an expected output, and an optional metadata dict. A scorer takes a prediction and a reference and returns a score between 0 and 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import Counter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class EvalCase:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, input_text, expected, metadata=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.input_text = input_text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.expected = expected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.metadata = metadata or {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class EvalSuite:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, name, cases, scorers):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.name = name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.cases = cases"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.scorers = scorers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def run(self, model_fn):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        results = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for case in self.cases:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            prediction = model_fn(case.input_text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            scores = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for scorer_name, scorer_fn in self.scorers.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                scores[scorer_name] = scorer_fn(prediction, case.expected)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            results.append({"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"input\": case.input_text,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"expected\": case.expected,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"prediction\": prediction,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                \"scores\": scores,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            })"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Scoring Functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Build exact match, token F1, and a simulated LLM-as-judge scorer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def exact_match(prediction, expected):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 if prediction.strip().lower() == expected.strip().lower() else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def token_f1(prediction, expected):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred_tokens = set(prediction.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exp_tokens = set(expected.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not pred_tokens or not exp_tokens:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    common = pred_tokens & exp_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    precision = len(common) / len(pred_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    recall = len(common) / len(exp_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if precision + recall == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 2 * (precision * recall) / (precision + recall)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def llm_judge_simulated(prediction, expected):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred_words = set(prediction.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exp_words = set(expected.lower().split())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not exp_words:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    overlap = len(pred_words & exp_words) / len(exp_words)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    length_penalty = min(1.0, len(prediction) / max(len(expected), 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return round(overlap * 0.7 + length_penalty * 0.3, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: ELO Rating System"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Implement pairwise comparisons with ELO updates. This is exactly the system Chatbot Arena uses to rank models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ELOTracker:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, k=32, initial_rating=1500):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ratings = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.k = k"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.initial_rating = initial_rating"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.history = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _ensure_player(self, name):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if name not in self.ratings:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.ratings[name] = self.initial_rating"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def expected_score(self, rating_a, rating_b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 1 / (1 + 10 ** ((rating_b - rating_a) / 400))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def record_match(self, player_a, player_b, outcome):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._ensure_player(player_a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._ensure_player(player_b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ea = self.expected_score(self.ratings[player_a], self.ratings[player_b])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eb = 1 - ea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if outcome == \"a\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            sa, sb = 1.0, 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif outcome == \"b\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            sa, sb = 0.0, 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            sa, sb = 0.5, 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ratings[player_a] += self.k * (sa - ea)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ratings[player_b] += self.k * (sb - eb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.history.append({"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"a\": player_a, \"b\": player_b,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"outcome\": outcome,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"rating_a\": round(self.ratings[player_a], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"rating_b\": round(self.ratings[player_b], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        })"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def leaderboard(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return sorted(self.ratings.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Perplexity Calculation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compute perplexity using token probabilities. In practice you would get these from the model's logits. Here we simulate with a probability distribution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def perplexity(log_probs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not log_probs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    avg_neg_log_prob = -np.mean(log_probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return float(np.exp(avg_neg_log_prob))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def token_log_probs_simulated(text, model_quality=0.8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    np.random.seed(hash(text) % 2**31)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = text.split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_probs = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, token in enumerate(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        base_prob = model_quality"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(token) > 8:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            base_prob *= 0.6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if i == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            base_prob *= 0.7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prob = np.clip(base_prob + np.random.normal(0, 0.1), 0.01, 0.99)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        log_probs.append(float(np.log(prob)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return log_probs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Aggregate Results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compute summary statistics across an eval run: mean, median, pass rate at a threshold, and per-metric breakdowns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def summarize_results(results, threshold=0.8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    all_scores = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for r in results:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for metric, score in r[\"scores\"].items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            all_scores.setdefault(metric, []).append(score)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    summary = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for metric, scores in all_scores.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        arr = np.array(scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        summary[metric] = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"mean\": round(float(np.mean(arr)), 3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"median\": round(float(np.median(arr)), 3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"std\": round(float(np.std(arr)), 3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"min\": round(float(np.min(arr)), 3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"max\": round(float(np.max(arr)), 3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"pass_rate\": round(float(np.mean(arr >= threshold)), 3),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"n\": len(scores),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return summary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def print_summary(summary, suite_name=\"Eval\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"\\n{'=' * 60}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {suite_name} Summary\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{'=' * 60}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for metric, stats in summary.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"\\n  {metric}:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"    Mean:      {stats['mean']:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"    Median:    {stats['median']:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"    Std:       {stats['std']:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"    Range:     [{stats['min']:.3f}, {stats['max']:.3f}]\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"    Pass rate: {stats['pass_rate']:.1%} (threshold >= 0.8)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"    N:         {stats['n']}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Run the Full Pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Wire everything together. Define a task, create test cases, simulate two models, run evals, compute ELO from pairwise comparisons, and print the leaderboard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def demo_model_good(prompt):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    responses = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What is the capital of France?\": \"Paris\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What is 2 + 2?\": \"4\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Who wrote Hamlet?\": \"William Shakespeare\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What language is PyTorch written in?\": \"Python and C++\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What is the boiling point of water?\": \"100 degrees Celsius\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return responses.get(prompt, \"I don't know\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def demo_model_bad(prompt):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    responses = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What is the capital of France?\": \"Paris is the capital city of France\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What is 2 + 2?\": \"The answer is four\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Who wrote Hamlet?\": \"Shakespeare\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What language is PyTorch written in?\": \"Python\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"What is the boiling point of water?\": \"212 Fahrenheit\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return responses.get(prompt, \"Unknown\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "cases = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    EvalCase(\"What is the capital of France?\", \"Paris\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    EvalCase(\"What is 2 + 2?\", \"4\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    EvalCase(\"Who wrote Hamlet?\", \"William Shakespeare\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    EvalCase(\"What language is PyTorch written in?\", \"Python and C++\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    EvalCase(\"What is the boiling point of water?\", \"100 degrees Celsius\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "suite = EvalSuite("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    name=\"General Knowledge\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cases=cases,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scorers={"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"exact_match\": exact_match,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"token_f1\": token_f1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"llm_judge\": llm_judge_simulated,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "results_good = suite.run(demo_model_good)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "results_bad = suite.run(demo_model_bad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print_summary(summarize_results(results_good), \"Model A (concise)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print_summary(summarize_results(results_bad), \"Model B (verbose)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The \"good\" model gives exact answers. The \"bad\" model gives verbose paraphrases. Exact match punishes the verbose model severely. Token F1 and LLM-as-judge are more forgiving. This illustrates why metric choice matters: the same model looks great or terrible depending on how you score it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: ELO Tournament"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run pairwise comparisons between models across multiple rounds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "elo = ELOTracker(k=32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for case in cases:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred_a = demo_model_good(case.input_text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred_b = demo_model_bad(case.input_text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    score_a = token_f1(pred_a, case.expected)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    score_b = token_f1(pred_b, case.expected)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if score_a > score_b:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        outcome = \"a\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    elif score_b > score_a:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        outcome = \"b\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        outcome = \"tie\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    elo.record_match(\"model_a_concise\", \"model_b_verbose\", outcome)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\nELO Leaderboard:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for name, rating in elo.leaderboard():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {name}: {rating:.0f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 8: Perplexity Comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compare perplexity across \"models\" of different quality levels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "test_text = \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog in the garden\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for quality, label in [(0.9, \"Strong model\"), (0.7, \"Medium model\"), (0.4, \"Weak model\")]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_probs = token_log_probs_simulated(test_text, model_quality=quality)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ppl = perplexity(log_probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {label} (quality={quality}): perplexity = {ppl:.2f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
